======================================================================
CHECK #1 — cell-body area confound (d7, qc-pass)
======================================================================

(a) cell-body size by condition (qc-pass cells)
           count  median   mean
condition                      
Control      434   153.7  170.0
KI           375   146.8  165.7
KO           500   144.9  153.1
    KO vs Control cell area: median 145 vs 154 µm²  (MW p=0.0179)
    KI vs Control cell area: median 147 vs 154 µm²  (MW p=0.569)

(b) does lyso size track cell area? (Spearman)
    pooled: rho=+0.206, p=5.45e-14
    Control : rho=+0.175, p=0.000254
    KI      : rho=+0.295, p=5.73e-09
    KO      : rho=+0.112, p=0.0119

(c) well-level (n=18): does KO deficit survive adjusting for cell area?
            lyso     area
condition                
Control    1.170  155.237
KI         1.466  159.358
KO         0.462  147.340

    RAW well-level KO-Ctrl lyso diff = -0.708 µm²
    AREA-ADJUSTED KO effect (OLS lyso ~ 1 + KO + area):
        KO coef   = -0.692 µm²  (SE 0.283, p=0.0369)
        area coef = +0.0021 µm²/µm² (SE 0.0136, p=0.882)
    -> if KO coef stays ~-0.71 and significant, the deficit is NOT a cell-area/clipping artifact.

